# isopod agent tint palette — which color each coding agent's terminal gets.
# Read by agent_preset(); the hex behind each preset name lives in share/colors.
#
# The point is telling four look-alike windows apart at a glance, so the colors
# are chosen to be distinct from each other rather than to match anyone's brand.
# Override one agent with ISOPOD_<AGENT>_COLOR (a preset name, '#rrggbb', or
# 'box' for the sandbox's own color), one run with --color, and turn the tint
# off with ISOPOD_AGENT_TINT=off or --no-color.
#
# agent     preset
claude      orange
codex       teal
opencode    blue
pi          purple
